[P_01_Lighthouse_CnvNoLacerda]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0001L=GERARDO: Did the boat get away okay?
Speech_0002L=IAGO: Si.  They've been gone for a while.
Speech_0003L=GERARDO: How many men went with them?
Speech_0004L=IAGO: Lacerda went.... and he took four others.
Speech_0005L=GERARDO: Hm... you'll be able to keep your guard up with four less men?
Speech_0006L=IAGO: No one will get by me, sir.

[P_01_Lighthouse_CnvRainPatrol]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0001L=DIEGO: Ay...it's sure coming down now...
Speech_0002L=IGNACIO: Si...well...you best get going then...
Speech_0003L=DIEGO: What? It's your turn to patrol...
Speech_0004L=IGNACIO: 'Turn' has nothing to do with it...it's about seniority.
Speech_0005L=DIEGO: Seniority? What? What is this, a union or something?
Speech_0006L=IGNACIO: Not yet... but once we topple the government, we'll form a union...so you best be on my good side now.
Speech_0007L=DIEGO: ...euh...fine...
Speech_0008L=DIEGO: ...ain't that always a way...eek out a living fighting for what you believe in and all you do is replace one oppressor for another...

[P_01_Lighthouse_CnvWeather]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0001L=DIEGO: You look troubled...
Speech_0002L=IGNACIO: Thunderstorms make me nervous...
Speech_0003L=DIEGO: Why?
Speech_0004L=IGNACIO: I was a boy in Grenada when the Americans invaded in '83. My father was in the army. When he realized we could not win, he led us into mountains with some of his men, and all of our families.
Speech_0005L=DIEGO: And?
Speech_0006L=IGNACIO: The Americans caught up with us one night in the middle of a thunderstorm... a thunderstorm like this one...
Speech_0007L=DIEGO: What happened?
Speech_0008L=IGNACIO: They struck in the dark... we never heard them... never saw them... they timed their fire with the thunder. The bodies dropped in the darkness. With each flash of lighting... there would be... more... corpses.
Note_0014L=The sound of thunder can be used to hide noises.
Speech_0009L=DIEGO: You survived... ?
Speech_0010L=IGNACIO: They left the women and children... no... the Americans are not butchers... but since that night... I have always been afraid of the thunder...
Speech_0011L=DIEGO: Well you're scaring me too...
Speech_0012L=IGNACIO: I know... as I said...  they are not butchers... their weapon is fear... and fear does not spread among the dead...
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0015L=(null)
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0016L=(null)
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0017L=(null)

